{"spec": "ollama:qwen2.5-coder:7b", "text": "```artifact\nFeature: Battery Management System\n\n  Scenario: GUI can compute battery ETA from a history of remaining battery amounts\n    Given a history of battery amounts [100, 90, 80]\n    When the GUI computes the battery ETA\n    Then the battery ETA should be 30 minutes\n\n  Scenario: GUI is connected to a battery amount sensor\n    Given the battery amount sensor is connected\n    When the GUI reads the battery amount\n    Then the battery amount should be within expected range\n\n  Scenario: GUI can compute a \"low battery\" alarm when battery ETA is <30min\n    Given a history of battery amounts [100, 50, 20]\n    When the GUI computes the battery ETA\n    Then a \"low battery\" alarm should be triggered\n    And the alarm priority should be low\n\n  Scenario: GUI can compute a \"critically low battery\" alarm when battery ETA is <10min\n    Given a history of battery amounts [100, 10, 0]\n    When the GUI computes the battery ETA\n    Then a \"critically low battery\" alarm should be triggered\n    And the alarm priority should be high\n\n  Scenario: GUI needs to have a \"battery failure\" alarm that is activated when the battery is absent, unavailable, or unchargeable\n    Given the battery is absent\n    When the GUI checks the battery status\n    Then a \"battery failure\" alarm should be triggered\n\n  Scenario Outline: GUI can compute battery ETA from different battery history lists\n    Given a history of battery amounts <battery_history>\n    When the GUI computes the battery ETA\n    Then the battery ETA should be <expected_eta>\n\n    Examples:\n      | battery_history | expected_eta |\n      | [100, 50, 10]   | 30 minutes   |\n      | [100, 50, 5]   | 30 minutes   |\n      | [100, 50, 100] | 0 minutes    |\n      | [100, 50, 0]   | 0 minutes    |\n      | [100, 50, 20]  | 30 minutes   |\n      | [100, 50, 80]  | 30 minutes   |\n      | [100, 50, 90]  | 30 minutes   |\n      | [100, 50, 100] | 0 minut